  "reason": "The current best is config_033 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, transformer, weighted; 0.713 acc). The most impactful untested variable in the multimodal pipeline is the image encoder: resnet50 alone yields only 0.208 acc in image-only mode, suggesting its features may be suboptimal. config_039 swaps resnet50 for imagenet_vit_l while holding all other settings at their known-best values (scvi_n200, multiprofile, transformer, weighted fusion). This is a clean single-variable experiment that directly tests whether a stronger, pretrained ViT-L encoder improves multimodal fusion. It is the best use of the next budget slot because it (1) extends the strongest evidence (config_033) along the most uncertain axis, (2) avoids re-testing already-clarified variables (fusion type, aggregation, RNA encoder), and (3) will inform whether further investment in image-encoder quality is worthwhile for subsequent experiments."
